  "result": {
    "text": "To complete the `decode_shift` function, you need to reverse the process used of the encoding by effectively shifting all the encoded characters back by 5 positions. Here's the complete implementation:\n\n```python\ndef decode_shift(s):\n\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes a string encoded with the encode_shift function and returns the decoded string.\n    \"\"\"\n    return \"\".join([chr(((ord(ch) - 5 - ord(\"a\")) % 26) + ord(\"a\")) + 5)  for ch in s])\n```\n\nThis function works by shifting each character in the input encoded string back by 5 positions in the alphabet. The `ord` function and `chr` function are alternately used to handle the character shifting.",
